6. Targeted read-only PowerShell log scan
Run on the Primary Site server in an elevated PowerShell window if access allows; change the log directory to match the actual installation. This only searches recent log lines and does not make changes.
$LogPath = "D:\Program Files\Microsoft Configuration Manager\Logs"
$Logs = @("RCMCtrl.log", "replmgr.log", "objreplmgr.log",
         "distmgr.log", "pkgxfermgr.log")
foreach ($Log in $Logs) {
   $File = Join-Path $LogPath $Log
   if (Test-Path $File) {
       Write-Host "`n===== $Log =====" -ForegroundColor Cyan
       Get-Content $File -Tail 300 |
           Select-String -Pattern "error|failed|exception|25H2" |
           Select-Object -Last 30
   }
}
After collecting the Package ID, CI Unique ID and Content ID, search complete logs for those exact values, not just generic error terms. Rotated historical logs may be needed.
